Installation and Execution

The Chicken Cross Road project is available on GitHub. Users can download the source code, compile the project, and run the game by following the steps below.

Step 1: Clone the Repository

Clone the project using the following command:

git clone https://github.com/nowshentanisha/Chicken-Cross-Road.git

Alternatively, users can download the project as a ZIP file from the GitHub repository and extract it.

Step 2: Install Java

Install Java Development Kit (JDK 21) or the required Java version.

Step 3: Open the Project

Open the project folder in Visual Studio Code, IntelliJ IDEA, or any Java-supported IDE.

Step 4: Build the Project

Compile the Java source files or use the IDE's build feature.

Step 5: Run the Game

Run the Main.java file to start the game.

Step 6: Play the Game
Click Start to begin the game.
Use the keyboard to control the player.
Avoid moving vehicles while crossing the road.
Cross the river safely by standing on floating logs.
Earn points as you progress through the game.
If the player collides with a vehicle or falls into the river, the Game Over screen will appear.
Select Restart to play again or Exit to close the game.
